":"https://i.discogs.com/fGUPZo_Cn7eFBVrNPJnG3ksKotj7bWLcU2kqCpb86dM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTM0OTEy/NTctMTc4OTQyMDM4/NS05OTI2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Electronic musician and DJ based in New York City.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3491257","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":14249128,"name":"Time Beats"}],"groups":[{"active":true,"id":4792348,"name":"Trackland Acid Track Squad"},{"active":true,"id":6258425,"name":"Hits Only"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Experience"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3491257-Ali-Berger","type":"artist","urls":["https://trackland.bandcamp.com","https://trackland.us","http://www.soundcloud.com/aliberger","http://www.youtube.com/user/alibergermusic","https://aliberger.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/40332/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"40332","image":"https://i.discogs.com/OPU-Pp49awdabk_lHUFPbJX78qv6thBadnLeDBTFd0o/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:534/w:523/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwMzMy/LTE3NzA0NTc5MzYt/MzQ1NC5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/km1sjvjjg21R0tN4giETSYEKrHVTcno1gb5C69PX3Og/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwMzMy/LTE3NzA0NTc5MzYt/MzQ1NC5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Seminal UK Punk band formed by [a=Pete Shelley] (1955-2018) and [a=Howard Devoto] in Bolton in February 1976. They start the band and chance upon a headline: \"It's The Buzz, Cock!\"\r\n\r\nApr 1, 1976: Pete Shelley - guitar, Howard Devoto - vocals, [a=Garth Smith] - bass, Mick Singleton - drums. \r\n- One gig. No released recordings.\r\n\r\nJul 20, 1976 - Feb 1977: Pete Shelley - Starway guitar, Howard Devoto - vocals, [a=Steve Diggle] (born 1956) - bass, [a=John Maher] - drums\r\n\r\nMar 11, 1977 - Oct 7, 1977: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, Steve Diggle - guitar, John Maher - drums, Garth Smith - bass\r\n\r\nNov 1977: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, Steve Diggle - guitar, John Maher - drums, [a=Barry Adamson] (on loan from MAGAZINE) - bass\r\n- Adamson filled in on bass while they held auditions for a permanent bassist. This lineup played 6 dates in November to complete a tour. No released recordings.\r\n\r\nNov 1977 - Mar 6, 1981: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, keyboards, Steve Diggle - guitar, vocals, John Maher - drums, [a=Steve Garvey] (born 1958) - bass\r\n- This is the line-up that released the 3 studio albums \"[m=13253]\", \"[m=13303]\" (both released in 1978), and \"[m=13283]\" (1979) as well as the classic singles compilation \"[m=13268]\" (with the exception that 2 songs feature Smith on bass instead of Garvey). They disbanded in 1981.\r\n\r\n(reformed) 1989, (reformed again) Jan 29 - Feb 18, 1992: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, keyboards, Steve Diggle - guitar, vocals, John Maher - drums, Steve Garvey - bass\r\n- The reformed group toured, but released no studio recordings. In 1992 they performed 11 gigs in Europe. There were no studio recordings.\r\n\r\nJan 31, 1990 - Dec 22, 1991: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, Steve Diggle - guitar, vocals, Steve Garvey - bass, [a=Mike Joyce] (ex VICTIM, ex SMITHS) - drums\r\n\r\nApr 21 - May 7, 1992: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, Steve Diggle - guitar, vocals, Steve Garvey - bass, Steve Gibson (ex ICICLE WORKS) - drums. \r\n- Ten gig tour in Australia and New Zealand. No released recordings.\r\n\r\nAug 25, 1992 - Apr 21, 2006: Pete Shelley - guitar, vocals, Steve Diggle - guitar, vocals, [a=Tony Barber] - bass, [a=Philip Barker] - drums\r\n- This line-up recorded and released five albums: \"[m=89019]\" (1993), '[m=321902]\" (1996), \"[m=215559]\" (1999), \"[m=89031]\" (2003) and '[m=89025]\" (2006)\r\n\r\nIn April 2005 Barker quit and was replaced [a=Danny Farrant] on drums. Barber quit in April 2008 and was in turn replaced by [a=Chris Remington] on bass. This line-up released the album \"[m=712923]\" in 2014. Pete Shelley passed away on December 6, 2018, and from then on theband continued with [a=Mani Perazzoli] as a touring member on guitars and backing vocals.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:40332","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":3240863,"name":"Stevie's Buzz"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":310589,"name":"Tony Barber"},{"active":false,"id":338774,"name":"Mike Joyce"},{"active":true,"id":395283,"name":"Steve Diggle"},{"active":false,"id":440262,"name":"John Maher"},{"active":false,"id":440263,"name":"Steve Garvey"},{"active":true,"id":545824,"name":"Chris Remington"},{"active":false,"id":706041,"name":"Garth Smith"},{"active":false,"id":910094,"name":"Philip Barker"},{"active":false,"id":1352835,"name":"Peter McNeish"},{"active":true,"id":2332779,"name":"Danny Farrant"},{"active":false,"id":5920590,"name":"Howard Trafford"}],"namevariations":["The Buzzcocks","«Buzzcocks»","バズコックス"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/40332-Buzzcocks","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.buzzcocks.com/","https://www.facebook.com/buzzcocksofficial","https://www.instagram.com/the_official_buzzcocks","http://www.secretpublic.com/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzzcocks","http://myspace.com/buzzcocksofficial","https://genius.com/artists/Buzzcocks","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BmTY6jMYu9s"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4058507/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4058507","image":"https://i.discogs.com/yZWzkTWTTt6amaz73AKFYfGIZPVf2cz0VO5IYCmM-MI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:399/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwNTg1/MDctMTQ0NjgyMDg3/MC05MDU5LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/h3BN7wN8Dfeqr06eSb6zlnjoqQw74aE-nvmydpM5BpA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQwNTg1/MDctMTQ0NjgyMDg3/MC05MDU5LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Ibeyi is a French/Cuban musical duo consisting of fraternal twin sisters, Lisa-Kaindé and Naomi Diaz, both born December 13, 1994 in Paris, France and founded 2013. The twins' father was the famed Cuban percussionist, [a=Miguel \"Angá\" Díaz] and their mother and manager is French-Venezuelan vocalist [a=Maya Dagnino].\r\n\r\nThe duo's sound combines Yoruban music with elements of jazz, pop, soul, gospel and hip-hop and the lyrics are sung in several languages including French, Spanish, Yoruban (from which the band's name derives. [i]ibeyi[/i]=\"twins\") and English. Lisa-Kaindé is lead vocalist and pianist while Naomi is the percussionist (cajón and batá).","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4058507","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":4218679,"name":"Lisa Kainde Diaz"},{"active":true,"id":4218680,"name":"Naomi Diaz"}],"namevariations":["雙生伊蓓"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4058507-Ibeyi","type":"artist","urls":["https://ibeyi.bandcamp.com","http://www.xlrecordings.com/ibeyi","http://www.bandsintown.com/Ibeyi","https://www.facebook.com/Ibeyi","http://instagram.com/ibeyi2","http://soundcloud.com/ibeyi","http://twitter.com/IbeyiOfficial","http://www.youtube.com/user/ibeyiofficial","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibeyi"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6858444/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6858444","image":"https://i.discogs.com/0fUmVEsfcsD0zIiyj8vy1k0R-5elP8ZxJ2_4-9E8Bb0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY4NTg0/NDQtMTc0OTM4NjU1/Ni00NDUyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/_AYl3ler9_7LynpzgQ0NNqOrPNIeGHs3Bn-XjmfsTKw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY4NTg0/NDQtMTc0OTM4NjU1/Ni00NDUyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Loraine James (London) is a British electronic producer and musician.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:6858444","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":10728985,"name":"Whatever The Weather"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/6858444-Loraine-James","type":"artist","urls":["https://lorainejames.bandcamp.com/music","https://soundcloud.com/lorainejames","https://twitter.com/LoJamMusic","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loraine_James","https://www.facebook.com/lorainejamesmusic"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/69544/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"69544","image":"https://i.discogs.com/TcWxLn42PnODVtJxaDknjgbRfZ27BPTLZNUMdr6eF7o/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:393/w:590/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY5NTQ0/LTE0NzEzNzI2MDAt/OTk2Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/4pLTjvy8U1nNDxoEnPqvGBIqNHzdUIEiqoTPxmdbp1k/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY5NTQ0/LTE0NzEzNzI2MDAt/OTk2Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Das EFX is a hip-hop duo consisting of [a=Andre Weston] aka [a=Drayz] (born November 2, 1970, in Teaneck, New Jersey) and [a=Willie Hines] aka [a=Skoob] (born November 27, 1970, in Brooklyn, New York). The two met while attending Virginia State University and formed the group during their college years.\r\nTheir breakthrough came after placing second in a talent show judged by [a=Parrish Smith] of [a=EPMD], who later signed them to the [a=Hit Squad (2)] collective. Das EFX gained recognition in the early 1990s for their debut album Dead Serious (1992), which introduced a distinctive lyrical style characterized by rapid delivery and playful word formations like \"diggety.\" The album was commercially successful and went platinum. They followed up with Straight Up Sewaside (1993) and Hold It Down (1995). \r\nWhile initially influential, the widespread imitation of their style by other artists eventually diluted their impact in the mainstream.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:69544","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":211386,"name":"Andre Weston"},{"active":true,"id":211387,"name":"Willie Hines"}],"namevariations":["D.EFX","DAS EFX","DAS-EFX","Da Efx","Das - EFX","Das E.F.X.","Das Efx","Das FX","Das Fx","Das-EFX","Das-Efx","DasEFX","DasFX","Dasefx"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/69544-Das-EFX","type":"artist","urls":["https://en.wikiped